-- title:
--   §4.1–§4.2 — randomized impulse game: randomizers and tie coins, plays, the profile ν*, deviations, payoff (22), subgame perfect equilibrium
-- statement:
--   The game layer of Kim and Kwon's impulse game of investment in a common good (§4.1–§4.2). Players are indexed by $i\in\{1,2\}$ (in Lean $0$ and $1$); $j$ denotes the opponent.
--
--   **Randomization devices** (p. 18). Each player $i$ has a randomizer $\hat l^{(i)}_m$ per period $m$, uniform on $[0,1]$, and each period has a fair coin deciding whose investment goes through when both players attempt at the same instant (the 50% rule). The Brownian motion, all randomizers and all coins are mutually independent, and the randomizers and coins are known at time $0$ to the state filtration.
--
--   **Plays** (pp. 17–18). A play from the state $x$ consists of the controlled state $X^\nu$, the investment times $0=T_0\le T_1\le\cdots$ (possibly $+\infty$), each player's attempted investment time $\tau^{(i)}_{m+1}\ge T_m$ in period $m=[T_m,T_{m+1})$, the boosts, and the player who invests at $T_{m+1}$. It must satisfy $T_{m+1}=\min(\tau^{(1)}_{m+1},\tau^{(2)}_{m+1})$, the earlier attempt goes through and the coin settles a tie, boosts are nonnegative,
--   $$X^\nu_t=x+\int_0^t\mu(X^\nu_s)\,ds+\int_0^t\sigma(X^\nu_s)\,dW_s+\sum_{m\ge1}\xi^\nu_m\mathbf 1_{\{T_m\le t\}}$$
--   with values in $\mathcal I$, and $T_m\to\infty$ almost surely.
--
--   **The profile $\nu^*$** (pp. 19–22), with threshold $\theta^*$, atom probability $q$, targets $z_1,z_2$ and rates $\lambda_1,\lambda_2$, from a starting stage $s_0\in\{1,2\}$ of period $0$. Let $\tau^m_{\theta^*}$ be the first time in $[T_m,T_{m+1}]$ at which the period's path (its pre-investment value at $T_{m+1}$) is at most $\theta^*$. The survival processes are $M^{(i)}_{m,t}=1$ for $t<\tau^m_{\theta^*}$ and, for $t\ge\tau^m_{\theta^*}$,
--   $$M^{(1)}_{m,t}=e^{-\int_{\tau^m_{\theta^*}}^t\lambda_1(X_s)ds},\qquad M^{(2)}_{m,t}=\big(1-\mathbf 1_{\{X_{\tau^m_{\theta^*}}=\theta^*\}}\,q\big)\,e^{-\int_{\tau^m_{\theta^*}}^t\lambda_2(X_s)ds}\quad(31)\text{–}(32),$$
--   where the atom of player 2 is available only in a first stage (every period $m\ge1$, and period $0$ if $s_0=1$). Player $i$ follows $\nu^*$ if in every period it attempts at $\inf\{t\ge T_m: M^{(i)}_{m,t}\le\hat l^{(i)}_m\}$ and boosts by $\max\{z_i-x,0\}$, $x$ the state at the time of investment.
--
--   **Deviations.** Player $i$'s behaviour is admissible if each attempt is a stopping time, and each executed boost is known at its time, for the information generated by the controlled path up to time $t$ and player $i$'s own randomizers.
--
--   **Payoff** (22): player $i$'s payoff is
--   $$\mathbb E\Big[\int_0^\infty\pi(X^\nu_s)e^{-rs}ds-\sum_{m\ge1}e^{-rT_m}(k\zeta^{(i)}_m+c_i)\mathbf 1_{\{\text{player }i\text{ invests at }T_m\}}\Big],$$
--   defined when the profit is integrable and the cost series is a.s. summable with integrable sum; the fair coin produces the factor $\tfrac12$ of (22) on simultaneous attempts.
--
--   **Subgame perfect equilibrium** (Definition, p. 7): from every state $x\in\mathcal I$ and either stage, every play of $\nu^*$ has well-defined payoffs, and for each player $i$, no play in which the opponent follows $\nu^*$ and player $i$ behaves admissibly gives player $i$ a larger well-defined payoff than a play of $\nu^*$.
--
--   These definitions let Theorems 2 and 3 be stated about the randomized game itself rather than about the analytic conditions that certify it.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Plays are characterized by relations and never constructed; no statement asserts that a play exists. The paper's filtration $\hat{\mathcal F}_t$ contains both players' randomizers; a deviating player is restricted to the controlled path and its own randomizers, which is the information the proof of Lemma B.6 uses (a deviator who saw the opponent's randomizer would know its investment time). "At any stopping time" in the SPE definition is read as Nash equilibrium of the subgame from every state and stage, which is how $\nu^*$ (Markov in state and stage) is analysed. The cumulative hazard is computed in $[0,\infty]$, so an infinite hazard means certain investment. The hitting time $\tau^m_{\theta^*}$ is taken on $[T_m,T_{m+1}]$ with the pre-investment state at $T_{m+1}$, so that an opponent investing exactly when $X$ reaches $\theta^*$ produces the tie the paper analyses.
-- source:
--   Kim & Kwon, Investment in the common good: free rider effect and the stability of mixed strategy equilibria, arXiv:2208.11217v1, pp. 7, 17–22, Definition (SPE), §4.1, §4.2, (22), (31), (32)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_InvestCommonGood_MixedTSSPE_Model

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Set
open scoped NNReal ENNReal Topology

namespace InvestCommonGood.MixedTSSPE

open VarContrib.RegularMPE

variable {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω]

/-- The opponent `j ≠ i` of player `i` (`0` is player 1, `1` is player 2). -/
def other (i : Fin 2) : Fin 2 := 1 - i

/-- The randomization devices of §4.1 (p. 18): the randomizer `l̂^{(i)}_m ∈ [0, 1]` of player
`i` in period `m`, and the tie coin of period `m` (the player whose investment goes through
when both attempt at the same time). -/
structure Rand (Ω : Type*) where
  /-- `L i m` is player `i`'s period-`m` randomizer `l̂^{(i)}_m` -/
  L : Fin 2 → ℕ → Ω → ℝ
  /-- `coin m` is the player who invests when both attempt at the same time in period `m` -/
  coin : ℕ → Ω → Fin 2

/-- The σ-algebras of the independent sources: the Brownian path, each randomizer, each coin. -/
def srcSigma (S : Setting Ω) (Rd : Rand Ω) : Option ((Fin 2 × ℕ) ⊕ ℕ) → MeasurableSpace Ω
  | none => MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω (t : ℝ≥0) => S.W t ω) inferInstance
  | some (Sum.inl p) => MeasurableSpace.comap (Rd.L p.1 p.2) inferInstance
  | some (Sum.inr n) => MeasurableSpace.comap (Rd.coin n) inferInstance

/-- The augmented probability space `Ŝ` of §4.1 (p. 18): every randomizer is uniform on
`[0, 1]` (Lebesgue measure), every tie coin is fair (the 50% rule), the Brownian motion, the
randomizers and the coins are mutually independent, and the randomizers and coins are
`ℱ₀`-measurable (so `(ℱ_t)` plays the role of `(F̂_t)`). -/
structure RandStanding (S : Setting Ω) (Rd : Rand Ω) : Prop where
  L_meas : ∀ i n, Measurable (Rd.L i n)
  L_unif : ∀ i n, Measure.map (Rd.L i n) S.P = volume.restrict (Icc (0 : ℝ) 1)
  coin_meas : ∀ n, Measurable (Rd.coin n)
  coin_fair : ∀ n (i : Fin 2), S.P {ω | Rd.coin n ω = i} = 1 / 2
  indep : iIndep (srcSigma S Rd) S.P
  L_F0 : ∀ i n, Measurable[S.ℱ 0] (Rd.L i n)
  coin_F0 : ∀ n, Measurable[S.ℱ 0] (Rd.coin n)

/-- A play of the impulse game (§4.1, pp. 17–18), described by its outcome:
* `X` the controlled state `X^ν` (right-continuous, post-jump value at investment times);
* `T m` the time `T_m` of the `m`-th investment (`T 0 = 0`; `⊤` if it never happens), so that
  period `m` is `[T m, T (m+1))`;
* `att i m` player `i`'s attempted investment time in period `m` (`⊤` = never);
* `boost i m` the boost player `i` executes if its period-`m` attempt goes through;
* `mover m` the player whose investment ends period `m`. -/
structure Play (Ω : Type*) where
  X : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ
  T : ℕ → Ω → WithTop ℝ≥0
  att : Fin 2 → ℕ → Ω → WithTop ℝ≥0
  boost : Fin 2 → ℕ → Ω → ℝ
  mover : ℕ → Ω → Fin 2

/-- The boost `ξ^ν_{m+1}` of the `(m+1)`-th investment (the one ending period `m`). -/
noncomputable def jump (O : Play Ω) (n : ℕ) (ω : Ω) : ℝ := O.boost (O.mover n ω) n ω

open Classical in
/-- The cumulative control `Σ_{m ≥ 1} ξ^ν_m 1{T_m ≤ t}` of the state equation (p. 18). -/
noncomputable def ctrl (O : Play Ω) (t : ℝ≥0) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  ∑' n, if O.T (n + 1) ω ≤ (t : WithTop ℝ≥0) then jump O n ω else 0

open Classical in
/-- The state just before the investment ending period `n`: `X` at `T (n+1)` minus the boosts of
that investment and of every later investment made at the same instant (`0` if `T (n+1) = ⊤`). -/
noncomputable def preState (O : Play Ω) (n : ℕ) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  match O.T (n + 1) ω with
  | ⊤ => 0
  | (s : ℝ≥0) => O.X s ω -
      ∑' k, if n ≤ k ∧ O.T (k + 1) ω = (s : WithTop ℝ≥0) then jump O k ω else 0

open Classical in
/-- The state path of period `n`: `X_t` for `t < T (n+1)`, frozen at the pre-investment state
from `T (n+1)` on. -/
noncomputable def perPath (O : Play Ω) (n : ℕ) (t : ℝ≥0) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  if (t : WithTop ℝ≥0) < O.T (n + 1) ω then O.X t ω else preState O n ω

/-- `τ^m_{θ*} = inf{t ∈ [T_m, T_{m+1}] : X_t ≤ θ*}` (p. 19), the first time the period-`m` path
(pre-investment value at `T_{m+1}`) is at or below `θ*`; `⊤` if there is none. -/
noncomputable def tauTheta (O : Play Ω) (θ : ℝ) (n : ℕ) (ω : Ω) : WithTop ℝ≥0 :=
  ⨅ t ∈ {t : ℝ≥0 | O.T n ω ≤ t ∧ (t : WithTop ℝ≥0) ≤ O.T (n + 1) ω ∧ perPath O n t ω ≤ θ},
    (t : WithTop ℝ≥0)

/-- Player 2's atom in period `n` (32): the period is in its first stage (`n ≥ 1`, or `n = 0`
and the game starts in stage 1, `s0 = 0`), `τ^n_{θ*} < ∞` and `X_{τ^n_{θ*}} = θ*`. -/
def atom (O : Play Ω) (s0 : Fin 2) (θ : ℝ) (n : ℕ) (ω : Ω) : Prop :=
  (n ≠ 0 ∨ s0 = 0) ∧ ∃ t : ℝ≥0, tauTheta O θ n ω = t ∧ perPath O n t ω = θ

/-- `e^{−a}` for `a ∈ [0, ∞]`, with `e^{−∞} = 0`. -/
noncomputable def expNeg (a : ℝ≥0∞) : ℝ := if a = ⊤ then 0 else Real.exp (-a.toReal)

/-- The cumulative hazard `∫_{τ^n_{θ*}}^t λ(X_s) ds` (in `[0, ∞]`) along the period-`n` path. -/
noncomputable def hazard (lam : ℝ → ℝ) (O : Play Ω) (θ : ℝ) (n : ℕ) (t : ℝ≥0) (ω : Ω) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ∫⁻ s in Icc (((tauTheta O θ n ω).untopD 0 : ℝ≥0) : ℝ) (t : ℝ),
    ENNReal.ofReal (lam (perPath O n s.toNNReal ω))

open Classical in
/-- The survival processes (31)–(32) of `ν*` in period `n` at time `t ≥ T_n`:
`M^{(i)}_{n,t} = 1` for `t < τ^n_{θ*}`, and for `t ≥ τ^n_{θ*}`
`M^{(1)}_{n,t} = exp(−∫_{τ}^t λ₁(X_s)ds)`,
`M^{(2)}_{n,t} = (1 − 1{X_τ = θ*} q) exp(−∫_{τ}^t λ₂(X_s)ds)` (the atom only in a first stage). -/
noncomputable def surv (q : ℝ) (lam : Fin 2 → ℝ → ℝ) (O : Play Ω) (s0 : Fin 2) (θ : ℝ)
    (i : Fin 2) (n : ℕ) (t : ℝ≥0) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  if (t : WithTop ℝ≥0) < tauTheta O θ n ω then 1
  else (if i = 1 ∧ atom O s0 θ n ω then 1 - q else 1) * expNeg (hazard (lam i) O θ n t ω)

/-- Player `i` follows `ν*(θ*, q, z, λ)` in the play `O` (§4.2, pp. 19–22), the game starting in
stage `s0` (`0`: stage 1, `1`: stage 2) of period 0: in every period `n`, its attempt is
`τ^{(i)}_{n+1} = inf{t ≥ T_n : M^{(i)}_{n,t} ≤ l̂^{(i)}_n}` (p. 18), and its boost is
`max{z_i − x, 0}`, `x` the state at the time of investment. -/
def FollowsStar (Rd : Rand Ω) (q θ : ℝ) (z : Fin 2 → ℝ) (lam : Fin 2 → ℝ → ℝ) (s0 : Fin 2)
    (O : Play Ω) (i : Fin 2) : Prop :=
  ∀ n ω, O.att i n ω =
      (⨅ t ∈ {t : ℝ≥0 | O.T n ω ≤ t ∧ surv q lam O s0 θ i n t ω ≤ Rd.L i n ω},
        (t : WithTop ℝ≥0)) ∧
    O.boost i n ω = max (z i - preState O n ω) 0

/-- `O` is a play from the state `x` (§4.1, pp. 17–18):
1. `T₀ = 0` and `T_{n+1} = min(τ^{(1)}_{n+1}, τ^{(2)}_{n+1})`, attempts not before `T_n`;
2. boosts are nonnegative; the earlier attempt goes through, and a tie is settled by the coin;
3. `X^ν_t = x + ∫₀ᵗ μ(X^ν_s)ds + ∫₀ᵗ σ(X^ν_s)dW_s + Σ_m ξ^ν_m 1{T_m ≤ t}` with values in `I`
   (published `IsStateSol`, initial state `X_{0−} = x`);
4. almost surely `T_n → ∞` (`lim_n η_n = ∞`, p. 17). -/
structure IsPlay (m : Model) (S : Setting Ω) (Rd : Rand Ω) (x : ℝ) (O : Play Ω) : Prop where
  T_zero : ∀ ω, O.T 0 ω = 0
  T_succ : ∀ n ω, O.T (n + 1) ω = min (O.att 0 n ω) (O.att 1 n ω)
  att_ge : ∀ i n ω, O.T n ω ≤ O.att i n ω
  boost_nonneg : ∀ i n ω, 0 ≤ O.boost i n ω
  mover_lt : ∀ i n ω, O.att i n ω < O.att (other i) n ω → O.mover n ω = i
  mover_tie : ∀ n ω, O.att 0 n ω = O.att 1 n ω → O.mover n ω = Rd.coin n ω
  state : IsStateSol m S m.μ x (ctrl O) O.X
  T_unbounded : ∀ᵐ ω ∂S.P, ∀ s : ℝ≥0, ∃ n, (s : WithTop ℝ≥0) < O.T n ω

/-- Player `i`'s information at time `t`: the controlled path up to `t` (which shows every past
investment) and player `i`'s own randomizers — not the opponent's randomizers, not the coins. -/
def info (Rd : Rand Ω) (O : Play Ω) (i : Fin 2) (t : ℝ≥0) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  (⨆ s : ℝ≥0, ⨆ (_ : s ≤ t), MeasurableSpace.comap (O.X s) inferInstance) ⊔
    ⨆ n, MeasurableSpace.comap (Rd.L i n) inferInstance

open Classical in
/-- Player `i`'s behaviour in `O` is an admissible (possibly randomized) strategy: every attempt
is a stopping time and every executed boost is known at its time, for player `i`'s information. -/
def IsDeviation (Rd : Rand Ω) (O : Play Ω) (i : Fin 2) : Prop :=
  ∀ n (t : ℝ≥0), MeasurableSet[info Rd O i t] {ω | O.att i n ω ≤ t} ∧
    Measurable[info Rd O i t] (fun ω => if O.att i n ω ≤ t then O.boost i n ω else 0)

open Classical in
/-- Player `i`'s discounted cost of the investment ending period `n`:
`e^{−rT_{n+1}}(kζ^{(i)} + c_i)` if it is player `i`'s, else `0` (`e^{−r·∞} = 0`). -/
noncomputable def costTerm (m : Model) (c : Fin 2 → ℝ) (O : Play Ω) (i : Fin 2) (n : ℕ)
    (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  if O.mover n ω = i then discAt m.r (O.T (n + 1) ω) * (m.k * O.boost i n ω + c i) else 0

/-- The payoff (22) of player `i` is well defined: discounted profit `P ⊗ dt`-integrable, the
cost series a.s. summable with integrable sum. -/
def PayInt (m : Model) (S : Setting Ω) (c : Fin 2 → ℝ) (O : Play Ω) (i : Fin 2) : Prop :=
  Integrable (fun p : Ω × ℝ => Real.exp (-(m.r * p.2)) * m.π (O.X p.2.toNNReal p.1))
    (S.P.prod (volume.restrict (Ioi (0 : ℝ)))) ∧
  (∀ᵐ ω ∂S.P, Summable (fun n => costTerm m c O i n ω)) ∧
  Integrable (fun ω => ∑' n, costTerm m c O i n ω) S.P

/-- Player `i`'s payoff (22) at time 0:
`E[∫₀^∞ π(X^ν_s)e^{−rs}ds − Σ_m e^{−rT_m}(kζ^{(i)}_m + c_i)1{player i invests at T_m}]`; the
fair tie coin gives the factor `1/2` of (22) on simultaneous attempts. -/
noncomputable def pay (m : Model) (S : Setting Ω) (c : Fin 2 → ℝ) (O : Play Ω) (i : Fin 2) : ℝ :=
  ∫ ω, ((∫ t in Ioi (0 : ℝ), Real.exp (-(m.r * t)) * m.π (O.X t.toNNReal ω))
    - ∑' n, costTerm m c O i n ω) ∂S.P

/-- `ν*(θ*, q, z, λ)` is a subgame perfect equilibrium (Definition, p. 7), read as a Nash
equilibrium of the subgame from every state `x ∈ I` and either stage `s0`: every play of `ν*`
has well-defined payoffs, and for each player `i` no play in which the opponent follows `ν*` and
player `i` uses any admissible strategy gives player `i` more than a play of `ν*`. -/
def IsSPE (m : Model) (S : Setting Ω) (Rd : Rand Ω) (c : Fin 2 → ℝ) (θ q : ℝ) (z : Fin 2 → ℝ)
    (lam : Fin 2 → ℝ → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ x ∈ m.I, ∀ s0 : Fin 2,
    (∀ O : Play Ω, IsPlay m S Rd x O → (∀ j, FollowsStar Rd q θ z lam s0 O j) →
      ∀ i, PayInt m S c O i) ∧
    ∀ i : Fin 2, ∀ Ostar O : Play Ω,
      IsPlay m S Rd x Ostar → (∀ j, FollowsStar Rd q θ z lam s0 Ostar j) →
      IsPlay m S Rd x O → FollowsStar Rd q θ z lam s0 O (other i) → IsDeviation Rd O i →
      PayInt m S c O i → pay m S c O i ≤ pay m S c Ostar i

end InvestCommonGood.MixedTSSPE


